---
import InfoPage from "~/components/InfoPage.astro";
import AboutTeam from "~/components/AboutTeam.astro";
---

<InfoPage
  title="Privacy | LostLink"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  subheading="What LostLink collects, who can see it, and why."
  description="LostLink privacy policy for the DLSAU lost and found system."
>
  <div class="mt-8 space-y-7 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-sage-700">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Your full name, your DLSAU email, and the item details you report (including
        photos you choose to upload). We do not collect phone numbers or any contact
        information beyond your school email.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Who can see it</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li>
          Approved listings show the item only. Reporter and claimant emails are never
          shown to other users.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your reports and claims are visible only to you and to the security office
          admins.
        </li>
        <li>
          Photos of IDs and Cards are hidden from the public listing. Only admins see
          the real photo.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Why we use it</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        To run the campus lost and found service: matching owners with found items and
        letting the security office verify claims. Your account is tied to your DLSAU
        email so claims are not anonymous. We do not use your data for anything else.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Storage and access</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Data is stored on Supabase with row-level security, so each account can only
        read what it is allowed to read. Access is limited to the LostLink service and
        the security office admins.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173), you may request a copy or
        correction of your data, or ask for your account to be removed. Visit the
        security office to make a request.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AboutTeam />
  </div>
</InfoPage>
